When to use which (senior perspective)
Use Declarative for 90% of your pipelines — microservice CI, Docker builds, Helm deploys, multi-branch pipelines. It's readable, team-friendly, and easy to audit in PRs.
Reach for Scripted when you genuinely need:
Dynamic stage generation (e.g., looping over a list of 20 microservices to create stages at runtime)
Complex Groovy DSL logic that when {} can't express
Legacy pipelines already written in Scripted that aren't worth migrating
Pro tip: You can also mix both — embed a script {} block inside Declarative steps when you need a burst of Groovy logic without rewriting the whole pipeline in Scripted.
stages {
    stage('Dynamic Logic') {
        steps {
            script {
                // Full Groovy power inside Declarative
                def services = ['auth', 'payment', 'notification']
                services.each { svc ->
                    sh "kubectl rollout status deployment/${svc}"
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
This hybrid approach is what most experienced teams land on in practice



